<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fundamental Orders of Connecticut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Fundamental Orders</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fundamental Orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> were adopted in January 1639 by the river towns of Hartford, Windsor and Wethersfield. They set out a government of an elected governor, magistrates and a General Court, deriving authority from the freemen rather than from a royal charter. They are often described as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1931-constitution-of-ethiopia">first written constitution</a> in the American colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fundamental-orders-of-connecticut.jpg" alt="Fundamental Orders of Connecticut" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Svgalbertian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Connecticut.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
